The letter-to-sound rules  (src/TS/speech_rules.py, made by tools/speech-rules.py)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

From NRL Report 7948, "Automatic Translation of English Text to Phonetics by
Means of Letter-to-Sound Rules" (Naval Research Laboratory, 1976), as John A.
Wasser coded them in english.c (1985, the CMU AI Repository's eng2phon
package). Both are public domain: a US-government report, and Wasser's own
"this is all public domain and I make no copyright claims on it".
